            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CasiBK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We found this delicious. I did make a few small changes based on the ingredients I had on hand. Rather than shaved ginger, I lightly coated each side with powdered ginger. I also toasted the sesame seeds before coating the fish. After adding the sesame oil I added kosher salt but no garlic pepper. Once the fish was just about done, I put it under the broiler for about 5 minutes to brown the seed crust on top. Just before serving, I poured a thin line of Trader Joe's Soyaki sauce down the middle of each piece. The fish was flavorful and juicy. Will definitely make it again."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rick's Recipes"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I like this recipe a lot. If you don't have sesame oil you can sub olive oil. It's best with the sesame oil. I rub the fresh ginger into the fish then put on the garlic pepper, drizzle with the oil. I also drizzle with tamari and some sweet mirin to heighten the Japanese flavors. Finally, I sprinkle the sesame seeds on top. Then bake as directed.",
            "datePublished": "2019-01-20T14:14:59.660Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
